<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Burkina Faso</h1><p class="st-meta">1960 CE – present · capital Ouagadougou</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Landlocked West African country, independent from France in 1960 as Upper Volta and renamed in 1984, with repeated coups and a jihadist insurgency since 2015.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-upper-volta">French Upper Volta</a> became a self-governing colony within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-community">French Community</a> on 11 December 1958, and attained full independence as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-volta">Republic of Upper Volta</a> on 5 August 1960. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-yameogo">Maurice Yaméogo</a> was the first president and banned all parties but his own.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The military deposed Yaméogo in 1966, and further coups followed in 1980, 1982 and 1983. Thomas Sankara took power on 4 August 1983 and renamed the country Burkina Faso in 1984, with a programme of vaccination, literacy and tree planting. Blaise Compaoré assassinated Sankara in a coup on 15 October 1987 and ruled until he resigned on 31 October 2014 after protests against an attempt to extend his rule. A coup by the presidential guard failed in September 2015.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Roch Marc Christian Kaboré won the 2015 election, but a jihadist insurgency that began in August 2015 grew, with 174% more armed violence in 2019 according to ACLED. Soldiers deposed Kaboré on 24 January 2022, and Captain Ibrahim Traoré ousted Damiba on 30 September 2022. In 2025 the army said it had foiled a coup attempt.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/burkina-faso.jpg" alt="Burkina Faso" width="330" height="220"><figcaption>Image: Drawn by SKopp , rewritten by Gabbe and Андрей Перцев · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Burkina_Faso.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1960 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ouagadougou</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Maurice Yaméogo, Sangoulé Lamizana, Thomas Sankara, Blaise Compaoré, Roch Marc Christian Kaboré</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam, Christianity, animist religions</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mooré, Dyula, Fula and Bissa, with French and English as working languages</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/burkina-faso">Burkina Faso</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Upper Volta, Republic of Upper Volta</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1993&amp;focus=burkina-faso" aria-label="Burkina Faso on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4638 1717 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Burkina Faso lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4958 1973L4958 1973"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4958 1973h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4958 1973h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4958 1973h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ouagadougou. <a href="/atlas?year=1993&amp;focus=burkina-faso">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
